Content:
Conditionally convergent sequences have a very different style to absolutely convergent sequences, in the sense that they `behave weirdly'. In particular, we cannot do the following to a conditionally convergent series (but we can to an absolutely convergent one).

\begin{itemize}
 \item Rearrange Terms (c.f. [REF:prop:ser-rearrangement-absolute-convergence] and Riemann Series/Rearrangement Theorem);
 \item Multiply series to a Convergent Product Series;
 \item Put Brackets on Terms (i.e. only studying a subsequence of partial sums).
\end{itemize}

