\begin{theorem}[Eisenstein's Criteria]

 Let \(R\) be a UFD, and \(f = a_0 + a_1 x + \cdots + a_n x^n \in R \bqty{x}\) be primitive, and \(a_n \neq 0\). If there is some \(p \in R\) which is irreducible, such that
 \begin{enumerate}
 \item \(p \notdivides a_n\);
 \item \(p \divides a_i\) for all \(0 \leq i < n\); and
 \item \(p^2 \notdivides a_0\);
 \end{enumerate}
 then \(f\) is irreducible in \(R\bqty{x}\), or equivalently, in \(F\bqty{x}\), where \(F\) is a field of fractions of \(R\) (by [REF:thm:gauss-lemma] (Gauss's Lemma)).
\end{theorem}

