\begin{remark}
 The Chinese Remainder Theorem can be extended to a system of congruences to more than 2 moduli. If \(m_1, m_2, \ldots, m_k\) are pairwise coprime, then for all \(a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_k \in \ZZ\), there exists a solution \(x \in \ZZ\) to the simultaneous congruences
 \begin{align*}
 x &\equiv a_1 \pmod{m_1} \\
 x &\equiv a_2 \pmod{m_2} \\
 &\vdots \\
 x &\equiv a_k \pmod{m_k},
 \end{align*}
 and such solution is unique modulo \(m_1 m_2 \cdots m_k\).
\end{remark}

