 \item For a proper convex value function, a supporting hyperplane exists at points in the relative interior of its effective domain. It need not exist at boundary points; for example \(\phi(c)=-\sqrt c\) on \(c\ge0\) has no finite supporting slope at zero, since such a slope would have to satisfy \(\lambda\le-1/\sqrt c\) for every \(c>0\).
 \end{itemize}
\end{remarks}

