\begin{theorem}[Supporting Hyperplane and Strong Duality with Dual Attainment]\label{optim-unit-0038}
    Assume the value function is proper and finite at \(\vb{b}\). Strong duality with dual attainment is satisfied if the value function \(\phi\) has a supporting hyperplane at \(\vb{b}\).

    Conversely, if strong duality holds for a suitable \(\vb*{\lambda}\), then \(\vb*{\lambda}\) is the supporting hyperplane to \(\phi\) at \(\vb{b}\).
\end{theorem}

