Type: prose
Local macros: \curl := \nabla\times; \div := \nabla\cdot; \grad := \nabla; \pqty := \left(#1\right)
Content:
Consider electric and magnetic fields \(\vb{E} \pqty{t, \vb{x}}\) and \(\vb{B} \pqty{t, \vb{x}}\). Two of Maxwell's Equations are
\begin{subequations}
 \begin{equation}

 \div \vb{B} = 0
 \end{equation}
 \begin{equation}

 \curl \vb{E} = - \pdv{t} \vb{B}.
 \end{equation}
\end{subequations}

Locally on a contractible spatial region, [REF:eq:b-curlless] tells us that \(\vb{B} = \curl \vb{A}\) for some \(\vb{A} \pqty{t, \vb{x}}\). Then putting this into [REF:eq:faraday] , gives us
\[
 \curl \pqty{\vb{E} + \pdv{t} \vb{A}} = \vb{0}
\]
and hence
\[
 \vb{E} = - \grad \phi - \pdv{t} \vb{A}
\]
for some \(\phi\pqty{t, \vb{x}}\). They are called the magnetic potential and electric potential respectively.

