\begin{proof}
Suppose $a,b \in \mathbb{R}$ are constructible. Then $a+b$ is constructible by construction (3), as is $-a$.

We can also construct $ab$ and $a/b$ using similar triangles %draw diagram of this.
\end{proof}

\begin{proposition}
If $a>0$ is constructible, so is $\sqrt{a}$.
\end{proposition}

