\begin{proof}
 We have
 \begin{align*}
 P R_a P^{-1}(x) &= P(P^{-1}(x) - 2(P^{-1}(x) \cdot a)a) \\
 &= x - 2(P^{-1}(x) \cdot a)(P a),
 \end{align*}
 but $P^{-1} = P^T$, so $P^{-1}(x)\cdot a = P^T x \cdot a = x^T P a$, which is just $x \cdot Pa$. So $P R_a P^{-1}(x) = x - 2(x\cdot Pa)(P_a) = R_{Pa}(x)$.
\end{proof}

