Content:
\begin{definition}[Valuation]
 A valuation is a function $v : L \rightarrow \{0, 1\}$ (where we think of $0$ as false and 1 as true) such that
 \begin{enumerate}
 \item $v(\bot) = 0$
 \item $v(p \Rightarrow q) = 0$ if $v(p) = 1$ and $v(q) = 0$, and $1$ otherwise.
 \end{enumerate}
\end{definition}

