\begin{remark}
 Officially, this says `let $(V, \in)$ be a model of ZF. Then [statement]. Equivalently, ZF $\vdash$ [statement] (by the completeness theorem).' Also from this proof, we know that in particular $x$ is contained in the transitive closure of $x$, the intersection of all transitive sets containing $x$, written $\operatorname{TC}(x)$ (as the intersection of transitive sets is transitive).
\end{remark}

