Content:
\begin{definition} 
$f:A\to B$ is
injective (one-to-one) if $f(a)=f(a')\imp a=a'$;
surjective (onto) if $f(A)=B$, i.e.\ every $b\in B$ equals $f(a)$ for some $a$;
bijective if both. When $f$ is bijective there is a unique inverse function
$f\inv:B\to A$ with $f\inv\circ f=\id_A$ and $f\circ f\inv=\id_B$.
\end{definition}

