Fix $x_0\in X$. The balls $H_m=N_m(x_0)$, $m\in\N$, cover $X\supseteq K$; a finite subcover
$H_{m_1},\dots$ has union the largest $H_M=N_M(x_0)$, so $K\subseteq N_M(x_0)$ is bounded.
