\item Suppose $f:\R\to\R$ satisfies $\displaystyle\lim_{h\to0}\big[f(x+h)-f(x-h)\big]=0$ for
 every $x\in\R$. Does this imply $f$ is continuous? (Answer with proof or counterexample.)
\end{exers}

