\begin{method}{Computing a residue}
Recognition. You need $\Res_{z=z_0}f$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Simple pole, $f=P/Q$ with $P(z_0)\neq0$, $Q$ simple zero: the slick formula is
 $\Res_{z=z_0}\frac{P}{Q}=\dfrac{P(z_0)}{Q'(z_0)}$ (since $Q(z)\approx Q'(z_0)(z-z_0)$).
\item Simple pole, general: $\Res_{z=z_0}f=\lim_{z\to z_0}(z-z_0)f(z)$.
\item Pole of order $n$: differentiate $n-1$ times as in Theorem~ [REF:t:resformula@c16] ;
 clear the pole first, then differentiate, then take the limit.
\item Unknown order / essential point: expand $f$ in a Laurent series and read off
 the coefficient of $(z-z_0)^{-1}$ directly.
\end{enumerate}
\end{method}

