The Eisenstein series satisfy:
(i) $E_k$ converges for $k\ge3$ and is holomorphic on $\HH$;
(ii) $E_k\equiv0$ if $k$ is odd;
(iii) $E_k(\tau+1)=E_k(\tau)$ and $E_k(\tau)=\tau^{-k}E_k(-1/\tau)$.
\end{theorem}

