The pentagonal numbers are $n=\tfrac{k(3k+1)}{2}$ for $k\in\Z$. The first few are
$1,\allowbreak 2,\allowbreak 5,\allowbreak 7,\allowbreak 12,\allowbreak 15,\allowbreak 22,\allowbreak 26,\allowbreak\dots$. (Triangular numbers are $\tfrac{k(k-1)}2$, squares are $k^2$.)
\end{definition}

