\begin{pitfall}
The maximal theorem is weak-type, not strong-type: $\norm{f^*}_{\Lone}\le
C\norm f_{\Lone}$ is false (Worked Example above). The correct strong bound is
$\norm{f^*}_{\Lp p}\le C_p\norm f_{\Lp p}$ for $1<p\le\infty$, obtained by interpolation;
at $p=1$ only the weak-type estimate survives. Also: the family of all rectangles
(not balls or cubes) fails both the weak-type bound and the differentiation theorem
(Problem~8) -- the geometry of the averaging family matters.
\end{pitfall}

