Type: theorem
Label: t:lebdiffloc@c26
Local macros: \Lone := L^1; \Rd := \mathbb{R}^{d}
Content:
\begin{theorem} 
If $f\in\Lone_{loc}(\Rd)$, then $\displaystyle\lim_{\substack{m(B)\to0\\x\in B}}
\frac1{m(B)}\int_B f(y)\,dy=f(x)$ for a.e.\ $x$.
\end{theorem}

