\begin{proof}
\begin{align*}
 S_N(f)(x)&=\sum_{n=-N}^N\hat f(n)e^{inx}
 =\sum_{n=-N}^N\Bigl(\frac1{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^\pi f(y)e^{-iny}\,dy\Bigr)e^{inx}\\
 &=\frac1{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^\pi f(y)\sum_{n=-N}^N e^{in(x-y)}\,dy=(f*D_N)(x).
\end{align*}
Interchanging the finite sum and integral is legitimate. So understanding $S_N(f)$ is
exactly understanding $f*D_N$.
\end{proof}

