\begin{proof}
$e_1=(\cos\alpha,\sin\alpha)$, $e_2=(-\sin\alpha,\cos\alpha)$ are an orthonormal pair in
$\C^2$, so for $Z=(a,b)$, $\abs Z^2=\abs{Z\cdot e_1}^2+\abs{Z\cdot e_2}^2$, which is the claim.
