\begin{definition} 
Let $G$ be a finite abelian group (written multiplicatively, with identity $1$). A
character of $G$ is a homomorphism $e:G\to\C^\times$ into the nonzero complex
numbers, i.e.\ $e(ab)=e(a)e(b)$ for all $a,b\in G$. The set of all characters is the
dual group $\widehat G$, with pointwise multiplication $(e_1e_2)(a)=e_1(a)e_2(a)$;
the trivial character $e_0\equiv1$ is its identity.
\end{definition}

