Content:
\begin{definition} 
Let $\mathcal P$ be the space of continuous functions $p:[0,\infty)\to\Rd$ with $p(0)=0$.
For $p,p'\in\mathcal P$ set $d_n(p,p')=\sup_{0\le t\le n}\abs{p(t)-p'(t)}$ and
\begin{equation} 
 d(p,p')=\sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{2^n}\,\frac{d_n(p,p')}{1+d_n(p,p')} .
\end{equation}
\end{definition}

