 \node[cglab,below left=2pt of j] {$j$};
 \node[cglab,below right=2pt of k] {$k$};
 \node[align=center] at (0,-2.6) {Forward arrows in the cyclic order $i\to j\to k\to i$ give a {\bf +}\\ ($ij=k$, $jk=i$, $ki=j$); going backward flips the sign to {\bf $-$}.};
\end{tikzpicture}


Reading the cycle $i\to j\to k\to i$: the product of two consecutive letters, in cyclic order, is the next letter with a $+$ sign; reversing the two factors flips the sign. Squaring any of $i,j,k$ gives $-1$.

