Type: method
Title: How to compute $\ord{x}$ in $Q_8$
Content:
\begin{method}{How to compute $\ord{x}$ in $Q_8$}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Compute $x^2$.
\item If $x^2=1$: then $\ord{x}\in\{1,2\}$; it is $1$ only when $x=1$, else $2$. (Only $-1$ has order $2$.)
\item If $x^2=-1$: then $x^4=(x^2)^2=(-1)^2=1$ and $x^2\neq1$, so $\ord{x}=4$.
\end{enumerate}
Recognition trigger. Every element of $Q_8$ squares to $1$ or $-1$. So the order is forced after a single squaring. There is NO element of order $3,6,8$ --- the only orders that occur are $1,2,4$, and $1$ and $2$ occur exactly once each.
\end{method}

