Type: method
Title: How to prove two finite groups are NOT isomorphic
Content:
\begin{method}{How to prove two finite groups are NOT isomorphic}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Compute a numerical invariant for both: most often the multiset of element orders (equivalently, ``how many elements of each order'').
\item Other invariants if the orders match: abelian?, size of the center, number of subgroups of a given order, is it cyclic?, exponent.
\item If ANY invariant differs, the groups are not isomorphic. (If all your invariants match, you have NOT proved isomorphism --- you must then exhibit an explicit isomorphism.)
\end{enumerate}
Recognition trigger. Use this whenever asked ``is $G\cong H$?'' for two concrete groups. For two non-abelian groups of order $8$, the order-$2$ count is the cleanest separator: $Q_8$ has $1$, $D_8$ has $5$.
\end{method}

