\begin{wex}{Chain lattice of $Z/(16)Z$}
Draw the subgroup lattice of $Z/(16)Z=\langle x\rangle$, $\ord{x}=16$.
\wrec
Cyclic group, so Proposition~ [REF:p:cycliclattice@c2] again: subgroups $\leftrightarrow$ divisors of $16$. Since $16=2^4$ has divisors $1,2,4,8,16$ that form a single divisibility chain, the lattice will be a straight chain (totally ordered).
\wsol
Step 1. Divisors $1,2,4,8,16$ give:
\[
1=\langle x^{16}\rangle,\ \langle x^8\rangle\ (\ord2),\ \langle x^4\rangle\ (\ord4),\ \langle x^2\rangle\ (\ord8),\ \langle x\rangle=Z/(16)Z.
\]

Step 2--3. Each order divides the next, and consecutive ratios are all $2$ (prime), so every consecutive pair is a covering and there are no incomparable subgroups:
\[
1\ \lessdot\ \langle x^8\rangle\ \lessdot\ \langle x^4\rangle\ \lessdot\ \langle x^2\rangle\ \lessdot\ Z/(16)Z.
\]
