Title: The lattice of $Z/(p^2)Z$ as a chain
Content:
\begin{wex}{The lattice of $Z/(p^2)Z$ as a chain}
Draw the subgroup lattice of a cyclic group $Z/(p^2)Z=\langle x\rangle$ of order $p^2$ ($p$ prime).
\wrec Cyclic of order $p^2$, so by Proposition~ [REF:p:cycliclattice@c2] subgroups correspond to the divisors
$1,p,p^2$, which form a single divisibility chain. This is the generic shape behind the concrete $Z/(16)Z$
chain already drawn; here we record the general $p^2$ picture.
\wsol The divisors of $p^2$ are $1,p,p^2$, giving exactly three subgroups:
\[
1=\langle x^{p^2}\rangle,\qquad \langle x^{p}\rangle\ (\ord p),\qquad \langle x\rangle=Z/(p^2)Z.
\]
Each consecutive ratio is $p$ (prime), so each is a covering and the lattice is a $2$-edge chain.
 \begin{tikzpicture}[yscale=1.0]
 \node[ltdot] (b) at (0,0) {};
 \node[ltdot] (m) at (0,1) {};
 \node[ltdot] (t) at (0,2) {};
 \begin{scope}[ltedge]
 \draw (b)--(m)--(t);
 \end{scope}
 \node[ltlab,below=1.5pt of b] {$1$};
 \node[ltlab,right=3pt of m] {$\langle x^{p}\rangle$};
 \node[ltlab,above=1.5pt of t] {$Z/(p^2)Z$};
