\begin{pitfall}
Index notation cuts both ways. $[G:H]=\ord G/\ord H$ is the number of cosets,
not a quotient group unless $H\nor G$. A set of $[G:H]$ cosets always exists;
the group structure on them ($G/H$) requires normality. Don't confuse ``$H$ has index $2$''
(always forces $H\nor G$) with ``$\ord H=2$'' (says nothing about normality).
\end{pitfall}

