The square below carries the dihedral symmetry group $D_8$: four rotations about its center $c$ (multiples of $90^\circ$) and four reflections, in the two diagonals and the two edge-bisectors. Two mirror lines, $\ell$ and $\ell'$, and the rotation center $c$ are marked; the reflection in $\ell$ and the quarter-turn about $c$ generate all eight symmetries.

\[
