Title: Determining the type of a wallpaper pattern
Content:
\begin{method}{Determining the type of a wallpaper pattern}
Trigger. You are handed a doubly periodic pattern and must name its point group (and ultimately its type).
\begin{enumerate}
\item Find the rotations. Locate the centers of rotational symmetry and the smallest rotation angle. This gives $n$ with the point group $C_n$ or $D_n$; by Theorem~ [REF:art:plane_groups:restriction@c4] , $n\in\{1,2,3,4,6\}$.
\item Reflection or glide? Look for mirror lines and glide lines. If the pattern has any reflection or glide symmetry, the point group is $D_n$; if it has none, it is $C_n$.
\item Distinguish same-point-group types. When $\overline G=D_n$, decide for each mirror direction in $\overline G$ whether it is realized by a true reflection (axis fixed) or only by a glide (no fixed line), and read off the lattice shape. This separates e.g. pm/pg/cm or pmm/pmg/pgg/cmm.
\end{enumerate}
\end{method}

