Type: theorem
Title: Classification of finite subgroups of $SO(3)$
Label: art:so3:main@c4
Content:
\begin{theorem}[Classification of finite subgroups of $SO(3)$] 
A finite subgroup $G$ of $SO(3)$ is one of:
\begin{itemize}
\item $C_k$, the cyclic group of rotations by multiples of $2\pi/k$ about a fixed line ($k$ arbitrary);
\item $D_k$, the dihedral group of the $2k$ rotations carrying a regular $k$-gon to itself;
\item $T$, the tetrahedral group of the $12$ rotational symmetries of a regular tetrahedron;
\item $O$, the octahedral group of the $24$ rotational symmetries of a cube (equivalently an octahedron);
\item $I$, the icosahedral group of the $60$ rotational symmetries of a regular icosahedron (equivalently a dodecahedron).
\end{itemize}
\end{theorem}

