 \node[ltlab,above=2pt of z8] {$Z_8$};
 \node[ltlab,right=2pt of z4] {$Z_4$};
 \node[ltlab,right=2pt of z2] {$Z_2$};
 \node[ltlab,below=2pt of z0] {$0$};
\end{tikzpicture}

(here $A_1,A_2,A_3$ are the three order-$2$ subgroups). The three atoms versus one atom distinguish the two abelian groups of order $8$: rank $2$ (invariant factors $2\mid 4$) gives a wide lattice with $(p^2-1)/(p-1)=3$ atoms, while rank $1$ (single invariant factor $8$) gives the single chain $0<Z_2<Z_4<Z_8$.
\end{exers}

