Title: Telling $Z/(2p)Z$ from $D_{2p}$
Content:
\begin{method}{Telling $Z/(2p)Z$ from $D_{2p}$}
Trigger. $|G|=2p$, $p$ odd prime. Always exactly two groups.
\begin{itemize}
\item Find $r$ with $\ord{r}=p$ (Cauchy) and $s$ with $\ord{s}=2$.
\item Compute $srs^{-1}$. If $srs^{-1}=r$ (commute): $G\congZ/(2p)Z$. If $srs^{-1}=r^{-1}$: $G\cong D_{2p}$.
\item Quick invariants: $Z/(2p)Z$ has an element of order $2p$ and is abelian with center $G$; $D_{2p}$ is nonabelian with center $1$ and has $p$ elements of order $2$.
\end{itemize}
\end{method}

