(2+3t)(1-t)=2\cdot1-2t+3t-3t^2=2-2t+3t-3=(2-3)+(-2+3)t=-1+t.
\]
\textit{Check.} Via the injective homomorphism $a+bt\mapsto(a+b,a-b)$ into $\mathbb{Z}\times\mathbb{Z}$: $2+3t\mapsto(5,-1)$, $1-t\mapsto(0,2)$;
product $(0,-2)$. Inverting, $a+b=0$, $a-b=-2$ gives $a=-1,b=1$, i.e. $-1+t$. Matches.
