\begin{pitfall}
Content lives up to units only. In $Z[x]$, $\cont(f)$ is determined up to sign;
in $k[t][x]$, up to a nonzero scalar in $k$. Do not assert ``$\cont(f)=6$'' as if it were
canonical without fixing the normalization ($\cont>0$ in $Z$, or monic in $k[t]$).
Likewise ``$\cont(fg)=\cont(f)\cont(g)$'' is an equality of associates.
\end{pitfall}

