\begin{definition}
Fix the variable order $x_1 > x_2 > \cdots > x_n$. Three standard orderings on $Z_{\ge 0}^n$:
\begin{itemize}
\item Lexicographic (lex): $\alpha >_{lex} \beta$ iff the leftmost nonzero entry of $\alpha-\beta$ is positive.
\item Graded lex (grlex): $\alpha >_{grlex}\beta$ iff $|\alpha|>|\beta|$, or ($|\alpha|=|\beta|$ and $\alpha >_{lex}\beta$).
\item Graded reverse lex (grevlex): $\alpha >_{grevlex}\beta$ iff $|\alpha|>|\beta|$, or ($|\alpha|=|\beta|$ and the rightmost nonzero entry of $\alpha-\beta$ is negative).
\end{itemize}
\end{definition}

