Type: method
Title: Applying the Submodule Criterion
Content:
\begin{method}{Applying the Submodule Criterion}
Recognition trigger: ``is $N$ a submodule of $M$?'' or ``show the following set is a submodule.''
\begin{enumerate}
\item Check $N\neq\varnothing$ --- usually by exhibiting $0\in N$.
\item Take arbitrary $x,y\in N$ and arbitrary $r\in R$ and show $x+ry\in N$ in one combined step.
\item One line replaces three (subgroup closure under $+$, under $-$, and under the action). For $F[x]$-modules this collapses to: $N$ is an $F$-subspace that is $T$-invariant ($TN\subseteq N$).
\end{enumerate}
\end{method}

