For three or more submodules, \emph{pairwise} trivial intersection $N_i\cap N_j=0$ ($i
eq j$) is 	extbf{not} enough for a direct sum. The correct condition is $N_i\cap ig(\sum_{j
eq i}N_j ig)=0$ for each $i$. Example in $M=\mathbb{R}^2$: lines $N_1=\mathbb{R}(1,0)$, $N_2=\mathbb{R}(0,1)$, $N_3=\mathbb{R}(1,1)$ meet pairwise in $0$, yet $N_3\subseteq N_1+N_2$, so $N_3\cap(N_1+N_2)=N_3
