Title: Computing $M\otimes_R N$ via the universal property
Content:
\begin{method}{Computing $M\otimes_R N$ via the universal property}
Trigger. You must identify a tensor product, or define / evaluate a homomorphism out of one.
\begin{enumerate}
\item To define a map out of $M\otimes_R N$: never define it on simple tensors directly. Define a balanced map $\varphi\colon M\times N\to L$, check all three balanced axioms, then the UP hands you $\Phi$ with $\Phi(m\otimes n)=\varphi(m,n)$.
\item To identify the group: guess the answer $T$, build maps both ways. Forward: a balanced $M\times N\to T$ gives $M\otimes_R N\to T$. Back: a map $T\to M\otimes_R N$ on generators. Check they are mutually inverse on simple tensors / generators.
\item To kill an element: exhibit it as $0$ using $0\otimes n=0$, $mr\otimes n=m\otimes rn$, and biadditivity --- relations only flow in this way.
\end{enumerate}
\end{method}

