\item $m\otimes n=0$ does \emph{not} imply $m=0$ or $n=0$. E.g. $\bar2\otimes\bar5=0$ in $\mathbb{Z}/(6)\mathbb{Z}\otimes_\mathbb{Z}\mathbb{Z}/(10)\mathbb{Z}$, and \emph{every} simple tensor is $0$ in $\mathbb{Q}\otimes_\mathbb{Z}\mathbb{Z}/(n)\mathbb{Z}$ or in $\mathbb{Z}/(2)\mathbb{Z}\otimes_\mathbb{Z}\mathbb{Z}/(3)\mathbb{Z}$.
