Title: Working with annihilators
Content:
\begin{method}{Working with annihilators}
Trigger. Compute $\operatorname{ann}(W)$, its dimension, or test membership.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Find a spanning set $w_1,\dots,w_k$ of $W$. Then $f\in\operatorname{ann}(W)$ iff $f(w_1)=\cdots=f(w_k)=0$ --- a homogeneous linear system in the coordinates of $f$.
\item The solution space has dimension $\dim\dual{V}-\rank(system)=n-\dim W$ (Proposition~ [REF:prop:ann@c11] ).
\item In coordinates: writing $W=\Span(columns of A)$, $\operatorname{ann}(W)$ is the left null space $\{f\in F^{1\times n}: fA=0\}$ of $A$.
\end{enumerate}
\end{method}

