\begin{wex}{Cofactor expansion of a $3\times 3$ over $Q$}
Compute $\det A$, $A = \begin{psmallmatrix} 2 & -1 & 0 \\ 1 & 3 & 4 \\ 0 & 2 & 1
\end{psmallmatrix}$, expanding along the first column.
\wrec Theorem~ [REF:thm:laplace@c11] ; column $1$ has a zero, easing the work.
\wsol
$\det A = 2\,c_{11} + 1\,c_{21} + 0$. Here
$c_{11} = (+1)\det\begin{psmallmatrix} 3 & 4 \\ 2 & 1 \end{psmallmatrix}
= 3 - 8 = -5$ and
$c_{21} = (-1)\det\begin{psmallmatrix} -1 & 0 \\ 2 & 1 \end{psmallmatrix}
= -(-1 - 0) = 1$. So $\det A = 2(-5) + 1(1) = -9$.
Sanity check. Expanding along row $1$:
$2\det\begin{psmallmatrix} 3 & 4 \\ 2 & 1\end{psmallmatrix}
- (-1)\det\begin{psmallmatrix} 1 & 4 \\ 0 & 1\end{psmallmatrix}
= 2(-5) + 1(1) = -9$. \checkmark
\end{wex}

