\begin{wex}{Determinant of a composite operator over $R$}
On $R^2$ let $R$ be rotation by $90^\circ$ and $S$ the shear
$\begin{psmallmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 0 & 1 \end{psmallmatrix}$. Find $\det(S R)$.
\wrec Theorem~ [REF:thm:det-operator@c11] : $\det(ST)=\det S\det T$.
\wsol $R = \begin{psmallmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 \end{psmallmatrix}$, $\det R = 1$;
$\det S = 1$. So $\det(SR) = 1\cdot 1 = 1$. Sanity check. Directly
$SR = \begin{psmallmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 0 & 1 \end{psmallmatrix}
\begin{psmallmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 \end{psmallmatrix}
= \begin{psmallmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 \end{psmallmatrix}$,
$\det = 0 - (-1) = 1$. \checkmark
\end{wex}

