\begin{corollary}[Positive definite $\Rightarrow$ split on every subspace]\label{art:orthogonality:posdef@c11}
In a Euclidean or Hermitian space the form is nondegenerate on every subspace $W$, so $V=W\oplus W^{\perp}$ for all $W$.
\end{corollary}

\begin{proof}
For any nonzero $w\in W$, $\langle w,w\rangle>0$, so $w$ is not a null vector of the restriction; the restricted nullspace is $\{0\}$, i.e.\ the form is nondegenerate on $W$. Apply Theorem~\ref{art:orthogonality:split@c11}.
\end{proof}

