\begin{remark}[{the module picture: $\Supp$ and $\Ass$}]
For a finitely generated module $M$ over a Noetherian ring, the support is $\Supp(M)=\{\fp\in\Spec R:M_\fp\ne0\}=V(\Ann M)$, the closed subset of $\Spec R$ where $M$ ``lives.'' It relates to $\Ass(M)$ by:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\arabic*)},leftmargin=*]
\item $\Ass(M)\subseteq\Supp(M)$, and the minimal elements of the two sets coincide;
\item $\Supp(M)=\bigcup_{\fp\in\Ass(M)}V(\fp)$, the union of the closed sets cut out by the associated primes;
\item the isolated primes of $\fa$ are the minimal primes of $\Supp(R/\fa)=V(\fa)$ --- recovering, for $R=k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ with $k$ algebraically closed, ``isolated primes $=$ irreducible components of $Z(\fa)$.''
\end{enumerate}
This is A\&M's geometric punchline: $\Ass$ records the embedded data, $\Supp$ records the underlying space, and the two agree exactly on the components.
\end{remark}

