\begin{theorem}[{regular local rings}]
Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring of dimension $d$ with maximal ideal $\fm$ and residue field $k=A/\fm$. The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)},leftmargin=*]
\item $\gr_\fm(A)\cong k[t_1,\dots,t_d]$ as graded rings;
\item $\dim_k(\fm/\fm^2)=d$;
\item $\fm$ can be generated by $d$ elements.
\end{enumerate}
A ring satisfying these is called a regular local ring, and a minimal generating set $x_1,\dots,x_d$ of $\fm$ is a regular system of parameters. The quantity $\dim_k(\fm/\fm^2)$ is the embedding dimension; regularity says embedding dimension $=$ Krull dimension.
\end{theorem}

