\begin{remark}
The characteristic assumption is essential for this formulation. Over
$F=\mathbb F_2(t)$, the polynomial $X^2-t$ is irreducible: the $t$-valuation
of a square is even, whereas that of $t$ is one. Its derivative is zero;
in $F(\sqrt t)$ it equals $(X-\sqrt t)^2$. This inseparable quadratic extension
has only the identity $F$-automorphism.
