\label{sec:introduction-to-group-theory}

There are two ways to view groups, \emph{algebra} and \emph{symmetry}. We first build intuition by looking at an example in symmetry, the equilateral triangle.

\begin{figure}[ht!]
    \centering

    \emph{No drawing was supplied in the source for this figure.}\par
