\begin{example*}[Equilateral Triangle]
    As in \autoref{fig:equilateral-triangle-symmetry}, an equilateral triangle has rotational symmetries and reflective symmetries.

    Note that there is the \emph{trivial symmetry} which is the \emph{identity}, that does not move the triangle and keeps it in place.

    An equilateral triangle has 6 symmetries, as listed in \autoref{fig:equilateral-triangle-symmetry-list}
\end{example*}

\begin{figure}[ht!]
